From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Klemm <github@tklemm.eu>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:40:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Look up attribute aliases with [] in resolve_attribute_name

`type_for_attribute` resolves an alias with
`attribute_aliases.fetch(name, &:itself)`, so every name without an
alias, the common case, calls the block through `Symbol#to_proc`.
`alias_attribute` and `define_id_value` only store Strings in the
frozen alias Hash, never `nil` or `false`, and the Hash has no default,
so `attribute_aliases[name] || name` returns the same object, as
`read_attribute` and the timestamp helpers already do.
---
 activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
index 5d36ad5f8d..8e033a6aec 100644
--- a/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
+++ b/activemodel/lib/active_model/attribute_methods.rb
@@ -423,7 +423,8 @@ def inherited(base) # :nodoc:
         end
 
         def resolve_attribute_name(name)
-          attribute_aliases.fetch(super, &:itself)
+          name = super
+          attribute_aliases[name] || name
         end
 
         def generated_attribute_methods
